Description

Alibaba has N boxes of treasure in front of him, each with a lot of coins. As much as he wants to open all the boxes, the boxes are password encrypted. Each password is a string of digits (where each digit is between 0 and 9).

Alibaba is given a group of digits to help him open the boxes. He can open only those boxes whose password can be formed using the digits provided to him.

The task is to determine the number of boxes he can open.

Input Format

The first line contains an integer T, denoting the number of test cases.

For each test case:

The first line of each testcase contains a string digits - the group of digits Alibaba is given to help him open the boxes.

The second line of each testcase contains an integer N - the number of boxes.

N lines follow where the ith line contains a string passwords[i] representing the password of the ith box.

Output Format

For each test case, output a single integer representing the number of boxes Alibaba can open.

Constraints

1 ≤ T ≤ 10

1 ≤ |digits| ≤ 10^4

1 ≤ N ≤ 100

1 ≤ |passwords[i]| ≤ 10^4

0 ≤ digits[i], passwords[i][j] ≤ 9

Sample Input 1

1
143
4
123
1111
13
143

Sample Output 1

2

Note

For the given testcase, he is given the digits "143", he can form "134", "314", "341", "413" or "431". He can also pick some of the digits and form "14", "13", "34", "1", "4" or "3".

Now, the boxes have passwords as "123", "1111", "13" and "143", he can open 2 boxes as he can only form "13" and "143".



Time Complexity per test case: O(N × M), where N is the number of boxes and M is the length of the longest password or digits string.


#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

void solve() {

    string digits;
    cin >> digits;

    vector<int> digitFreq(10, 0);

    // frequency of available digits
    for(char c : digits) {
        digitFreq[c - '0']++;
    }

    int pass;
    cin >> pass;

    int cnt = 0;

    while(pass--) {

        string password;
        cin >> password;

        vector<int> passFreq(10, 0);

        bool flag = false;

        for(char c : password) {

            passFreq[c - '0']++;

            // if required freq exceeds available freq
            if(passFreq[c - '0'] > digitFreq[c - '0']) {
                flag = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        if(!flag)
            cnt++;
    }

    cout << cnt << endl;
}

int main() {

    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;

    while(t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}
